<main id="main"><div class="container"><nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><ol><li><a href="index.html">Home</a></li><li aria-current="page"><span>Foreign National Mortgage Options in Miami</span></li></ol></nav></div><section class="hero"><div class="container hero-grid"><div class="hero-copy"><p class="eyebrow">International buyer financing</p><h1>Foreign National Mortgage Options in Miami</h1><p>Financing guidance for international buyers purchasing Miami condos, second homes, and investment properties.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="btn btn-primary" href="start.html">Discuss Foreign Buyer Options</a><a class="btn btn-secondary" href="mortgage-calculator-florida.html">Start Review</a></div><div class="trust-row"><span class="trust-pill">Matthew Gromadzki</span><span class="trust-pill">NMLS #2560919</span><span class="trust-pill">Miami · Florida</span><span class="trust-pill">Call (305) 988-4806</span></div></div><div class="hero-panel rate-card"><div class="rate-item"><span>Best first step</span><strong>Preapproval</strong></div><div class="rate-item"><span>Core review</span><strong>Payment + cash to close</strong></div><div class="rate-item"><span>Miami focus</span><strong>Condo + jumbo checks</strong></div><a class="btn btn-primary full" href="start.html">Send Scenario</a></div></div></section><section class="section"><div class="container two-col"><article class="prose"><p>Miami attracts buyers from around the world. Foreign national mortgage options may be available for eligible non-U.S. buyers, but documentation, down payment, reserves, property type, and country-specific details can vary significantly.</p><p>A mortgage broker can help compare programs and clarify what documents are needed before a buyer travels, wires funds, or signs a purchase contract.</p><h2>What lenders may review</h2><p>A lender may review passport or visa status, income documentation, bank statements, credit references, assets, reserves, source of funds, property type, occupancy, and loan amount.</p><p>For condos, the building must also be reviewed. This is particularly important for waterfront and luxury high-rise properties.</p><h2>Planning before contract</h2><p>International buyers should review financing before contract deadlines. Down payment, wire timing, entity structure, reserves, title requirements, and foreign currency transfer timing can all affect the process.</p><p>A written scenario review can help buyers and agents know what is realistic before negotiations begin.</p></article><aside><form class="lead-form lead-form-compact" method="post" action="quote.html" data-lead-form><h2>Request a Foreign National Mortgage Options Miami Quote</h2><p>Answer a few basics and we’ll review the best mortgage path for your scenario.</p><input type="hidden" name="source_page" value="preview"><label>Loan goal<select name="loan_goal" required><option value="">Select one</option><option>Buying a home</option><option>Refinancing</option><option>Cash-out refinance</option><option>Investment property</option><option>Condo financing</option></select></label><div class="form-row"><label>Purchase price / value<input name="property_value" inputmode="numeric" placeholder="$650,000"></label><label>Down payment / equity<input name="down_payment" inputmode="numeric" placeholder="$100,000"></label></div><div class="form-row"><label>Credit score range<select name="credit_score"><option value="">Select range</option><option>760+</option><option>720–759</option><option>680–719</option><option>640–679</option><option>Below 640</option><option>Not sure</option></select></label><label>Property city<input name="property_city" placeholder="Miami"></label></div><div class="form-row"><label>Name<input name="name" autocomplete="name" required></label><label>Phone<input name="phone" autocomplete="tel" required></label></div><label>Email<input name="email" type="email" autocomplete="email" required></label><button class="btn btn-primary full" type="submit">Start Mortgage Review</button><p class="form-note">No obligation. Mortgage options depend on underwriting, lender guidelines, property type, and documentation.</p></form></aside></div></section><section class="section soft"><div class="container"><div class="cta-band"><div><p class="eyebrow">Fast next step</p><h2>Get a mortgage scenario review before you make a decision.</h2><p>Send purchase price, down payment, credit range, income type, and property city. The goal is to compare real options, not guess based on generic rates.</p></div><div class="hero-actions"><a class="btn btn-primary" href="start.html">Start Review</a><a class="btn btn-secondary" href="tel:+13059884806">Call (305) 988-4806</a></div></div></div></section><section class="section faq-section"><div class="container narrow"><p class="eyebrow">Questions</p><h2>Foreign National Mortgage Options in Miami FAQ</h2><div class="faq-list"><details><summary>Can a non-U.S. citizen get a mortgage in Miami?</summary><p>Foreign national mortgage options may be available, depending on documentation, down payment, assets, country, property type, and lender guidelines.</p></details><details><summary>Can foreign nationals finance condos?</summary><p>Sometimes. The condo project and borrower documentation both need to be reviewed.</p></details><details><summary>Do foreign national loans require larger down payments?</summary><p>Many programs require stronger down payment and reserves than standard domestic borrower programs, but options vary.</p></details></div></div></section><section class="section related-section"><div class="container"><p class="eyebrow">Keep comparing</p><h2>Related mortgage pages</h2><div class="card-grid small-grid"><a class="mini-card" href="jumbo-loans-miami.html">Jumbo Loans Miami<span>→</span></a><a class="mini-card" href="condo-loans-miami.html">Condo Loans Miami<span>→</span></a><a class="mini-card" href="mortgage-broker-miami-beach.html">Mortgage Broker Miami Beach<span>→</span></a><a 